    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Crown rule replaced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> in 1858, after the rebellion of 1857, and lasted until independence in 1947.</li><li>A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> ruled British provinces directly and more than 560 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> indirectly, with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-civil-service">Indian Civil Service</a> at its core.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi">Gandhi</a>’s mass campaigns and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> ended British rule, and partition into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> cost hundreds of thousands of lives.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-army">Indian Army</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, about 2.5 million strong, is often described as the largest all-volunteer army in history.</p></aside>
    </section>

