ple at the Jallianwala Bagh in Amritsar</title></g><g class="rf-ev"><line x1="602.5" x2="602.5" y1="160" y2="166"/><circle cx="602.5" cy="160" r="8"/><text x="602.5" y="164" text-anchor="middle">6</text><title>1930: Gandhi leads the Salt March to Dandi</title></g><g class="rf-ev"><line x1="699.6" x2="699.6" y1="160" y2="166"/><circle cx="699.6" cy="160" r="8"/><text x="699.6" y="164" text-anchor="middle">7</text><title>1942: Congress launches the Quit India movement</title></g><g class="rf-ev"><line x1="740.0" x2="740.0" y1="160" y2="166"/><circle cx="740.0" cy="160" r="8"/><text x="740.0" y="164" text-anchor="middle">8</text><title>1947: Independence and partition create India and Pakistan on 14–15 August</title></g><text class="rf-axis" x="20" y="200">1858 CE</text><text class="rf-axis" x="740" y="200" text-anchor="end">1947 CE</text></svg><figcaption>Relative power on the Institute's 0–10 scale (each profile scaled to its own peak). Numbers mark the key events below.</figcaption></figure><ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">1858</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/government-of-india">Government of India</a> Act transfers the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a>’s territories to the Crown</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1877</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/queen-victoria">Queen Victoria</a> is proclaimed Empress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-durbar">Delhi Durbar</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1885</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-national-congress">Indian National Congress</a> is founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mumbai">Bombay</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1911</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-v">George V</a> announces the move of the capital from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kolkata">Calcutta</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1919</span><span class="rf-text">Troops kill hundreds of unarmed people at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jallianwala-bagh-massacre">Jallianwala Bagh</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amritsar">Amritsar</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1930</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi">Gandhi</a> leads the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salt-march">Salt March</a> to Dandi</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1942</span><span class="rf-text">Congress launches the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quit-india-movement">Quit India</a> movement</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1947</span><span class="rf-text">Independence and partition create <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> on 14–15 August</span></li></ol>
